# Part II — Additional Terms to the PolyForm Free Trial License 1.0.0

Copyright (c) 2025 OpenHappy Team

These Additional Terms are conditions of the license granted to you for OpenHappy (the "software").
They are part of that license. Where they conflict with the license text in Part I, these
Additional Terms prevail.

## 1. Scope: source code and design documents only

The licensed material — everything these terms and Part I grant rights in, and everything
Sections 2 to 5 restrict — is limited to:

- the **source code** in this repository: the RTL and testbench sources under `code/` and `verify/`,
  together with their filelists, macro files, scripts and build files;
- the **design documents** in this repository: the Markdown documents under `docs/` and the documents
  in the repository root (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `NOTICE`, these Additional Terms).

Nothing else is licensed, claimed or restricted. In particular:

- the standard this project is written against, and the protocol, interface, register and pin
  definitions it describes, are **not** licensed material — they belong to their own authors;
- ideas, methods, algorithms and know-how are not licensed material;
- your own designs, RTL, software, testbenches, integration code, tooling and products are not
  licensed material, even where they interoperate with or are built using the software;
- simulation outputs, waveforms, logs, coverage data, synthesis and place-and-route results, masks and
  fabricated silicon are not licensed material.

## 2. No modification without prior written authorization

The license text in Part I contains a "Changes and New Works License". You do not receive that
grant unless OpenHappy Team has given you prior written authorization. Without that authorization you
may not modify, adapt, translate, refactor, re-parameterize or otherwise create a derivative of the
licensed material — including local bug fixes, macro changes and RTL or testbench changes — and you
may not have anyone do so on your behalf.

Request that authorization in writing from OpenHappy Team. This repository has no public ordering
channel.

## 3. Configuration exception

Configuring your local copy to run the shipped flow is not a modification and needs no separate
authorization. Permitted configuration is limited to:

- setting environment variables (`PROJ_HOME`, `HIPINEXT_HOME`, `D2D_HIPI_DV_HOME`, `D2D_SIM_HOME`, and
  the compatibility alias `HIPI_NEXT_HOME`) instead of editing any file;
- adjusting the path, tool-location and waveform-viewer variables documented in
  `docs/UserGuide.md` §3.1 (`verify/env.sh`, `verify/Makefile`, `verify/script/run.sh`,
  `verify/script/open_wave.sh`) so the flow finds your Verilator, C++ compiler, make and viewer;
- passing the existing make or script arguments provided for that purpose (for example
  `VERILATOR=<path>`, `TEST=`, `LOOPBACK=`, `TRAIN_BYPASS=`).

Configuration under this section must not change RTL, testbench or filelist content, must not change
the compile configuration in `code/design/rtl_v/top/hipi_top_defines.vh`, and must not be distributed.

## 4. Intellectual property in derivatives of the licensed material

All intellectual property rights in any authorized modification of, or derivative work based on, the
licensed material — including copyright, patents, utility models and mask-work (layout-design) rights
in so far as they cover that material or those modifications — vest in OpenHappy Team on creation. To
the extent such rights cannot vest automatically under applicable law, you assign them to OpenHappy
Team on creation and will execute any document OpenHappy Team reasonably requests to perfect that
assignment.

This section reaches only rights in the licensed material and in modifications and derivatives of it.
It does not reach anything listed as outside the scope in Section 1.

You may not file, or cause to be filed, any patent or utility-model application covering an
authorized modification or a derivative of the licensed material without OpenHappy Team's prior
written consent.

## 5. Your own material stays yours

Rights you already held before receiving the software — including your own specifications,
testbenches, integration code, tooling and products — are unaffected by these Additional Terms, and
nothing you create independently falls under Section 4.

## 6. Patent license unchanged

The `## Patent License` grant and the `## Patent Defense` clause in Part I are not narrowed,
restricted or revoked by these Additional Terms.

## 7. Everything else unchanged

All other terms of the PolyForm Free Trial License 1.0.0 remain in force, including the evaluation
window of less than 32 consecutive calendar days, the prohibition on distribution, and the "as is"
disclaimer with its limitation of liability.
